okbook:Mincing|minced]]\n*¼ cup [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]] [[cookbook:Onion|white onion]]\n*¼ cup [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[cookbook:Green onion|green onion]]\n*2 whole [[cookbook:clove|cloves]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] ground [[cookbook:cumin|cumin]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] caribe or another ground [[cookbook:Chili Pepper|hot pepper]]\n*Juice of 1 [[cookbook:lime|lime]]\n*[[cookbook:salt|Salt]] to taste\n*[[cookbook:pepper|Pepper]] to taste\n\n==Procedure==\n# Place beans in a large pan and cover with water. Bring to a [[cookbook:boil|boil]] and remove from heat. Cover and let stand for 1 hour. [[cookbook:Simmer|Simmer]] for 2 hours and drain.\n# Place beans in a large pan and add 8 cups water, garlic, salt, white onions, cumin, ground chili and lime juice. Tie cloves in [[Cookbook:Cheesecloth|cheesecloth]] for easy removal if desired. Bring to a boil; reduce heat, cover and simmer for 2 hours or until beans are tender and soup is thick.\n# Mix in green onions and serve with lime wedge.\n\n[[Category:Vegan recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes for soup|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using black bean|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Brazilian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lime juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green onion]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Brazilian Black Bean Soup","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"4–6","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 cups dried black beans","sourceText":"2 cups dried black beans","amountText":"2 cups dried black beans","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"8 cups water","sourceText":"8 cups water","amountText":"8 cups water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"4 clove